kev  (planned: vendored subset)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:  https://github.com/jaredpalmer/kev
License: Apache License 2.0
Author:  Jared Palmer

Status: NOT YET VENDORED. This entry is a placeholder for the planned vendoring of
kev's inference kernel into src/decis/engines/_kev_vendor/.

When vendoring is performed, this entry MUST be updated with:
  - the exact commit SHA that was pinned
  - the list of files copied
  - any local modifications made to those files

The intended subset is limited to the inference path:
  kev/model.py      -> encode(), branch_mask_batch(), PointerHead, DecisionModel
  kev/checkpoint.py -> Checkpoint, Meta, LoadOptions
kev/api.py is deliberately NOT vendored: Decis implements the wire contract in
src/decis/answers.py so that every engine shares one answer/confidence definition.
kev's training, evaluation and dataset modules are not used.

